{
  "Name": "Hallows_Eve_Old_Jack",
  "$Comment": [
    "Old Jack's conversation, everything he says at the Forgotten Temple while Hallow's Eve runs.",
    "He contracts everything he says: I'm, it's, don't.",
    "",
    "HOW A SCREEN IS PICKED. Start is walked in a fixed order: First (top to bottom), then a quest",
    "that is READY to hand in, then one he can OFFER, then one that is ACTIVE, then Then, then",
    "Fallback. First holds the greeting, shown until the hail spends it, and the board line, shown",
    "once a day (Once with Period Daily, turning over at midnight UTC) and skipped while the player",
    "has something to hand in. Quests holds one row per quest, the questline first, so the questline",
    "wins a tie with a daily. Then shows the lit-lantern line once the year's lantern is lit.",
    "",
    "THE BOARD LINE AND FAVOR. The board line comes in four wordings, one per band of favor with",
    "Old Jack, highest first, so the first that applies is the player's own rank: Revered, Honored,",
    "Friendly, then the plain one, which is also what shows while the reputation is switched off.",
    "All four share one daily Once through OnceId, so whichever wording a player hears spends the",
    "line for the day, and a rank climbed later that day does not bring it back. Their Actions pay",
    "a little favor with Old Jack (the Reputation reward; Amount is how much) when the player",
    "finishes the line, whichever way they leave it: an answer, trick-or-treat or goodbye.",
    "",
    "THE FOOTER. Most screens pull in the jack_footer group: hand-ins, the quest list, the board, the",
    "stall, How do we stand? (it opens the Reputation page, and shows once the player has any favor",
    "with him), the Almanac (only while the Almanac is switched on), two lore lines, the Harvest Moon",
    "line (only while Harvest Moon runs) and goodbye. The trick-or-treat line is not here: it comes",
    "from the DialogueExtensions file Hallows_Eve_Trick_Or_Treat, which adds it to every",
    "conversation, this one included.",
    "",
    "The greeting's memory is kept per world family, ForgottenTemple, the one place he stands."
  ],
